      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 2.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve the non-linear system: \\( y=x^2 \\) and \\( y=x+2 \\). \\[ x^2=x+2 \\implies x^2-x-2=0 \\implies (x-2)(x+1)=0 \\implies x=2 \\text{ or } x=-1. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Logarithms & Exponential Equations",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Key log laws: \\(\\log_b(xy) = \\log_b x + \\log_b y\\); \\(\\log_b(x/y) = \\log_b x - \\log_b y\\); \\(\\log_b(x^n) = n\\log_b x\\). To solve \\(a^{f(x)} = b\\): take \\(\\log\\) of both sides. Change of base: \\(\\log_b x = \\dfrac{\\ln x}{\\ln b}\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Solving a logarithmic equation",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve \\(\\log_2(x+3) + \\log_2(x-1) = 5\\). <p>\\(\\log_2[(x+3)(x-1)] = 5 \\Rightarrow (x+3)(x-1) = 32 \\Rightarrow x^2+2x-35 = 0 \\Rightarrow (x+7)(x-5) = 0\\).</p><p>\\(x = 5\\) (reject \\(x=-7\\) since \\(x-1 > 0\\) required). Answer: \\(x=5\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Solve for \\(x\\): \\(3^{x+1} = 5^x\\). Give your answer in terms of logarithms.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Take \\(\\ln\\): \\((x+1)\\ln 3 = x\\ln 5 \\Rightarrow x\\ln 3 + \\ln 3 = x\\ln 5 \\Rightarrow x = \\dfrac{\\ln 3}{\\ln 5 - \\ln 3} = \\dfrac{\\ln 3}{\\ln(5/3)}\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
